# ── Never commit: credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every project reads its own .env. Between them these hold the Postgres URL,
# the Vercel Blob read/write token, the links-export token, the captcha API key
# and the auth secret — a push of any one of them is a credential leak that
# survives in the history even after a delete.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
local.properties

# ── Never commit: live logged-in browser sessions ────────────────────────────
# These are not caches. A Chromium user data directory is a signed-in browser:
# cookies, tokens and the device fingerprint TikTok/Instagram derive from it.
# Anyone with the folder is logged in as those accounts.
profile/
profile-*/
browser_profile/
captcha-dump/

# ── Never commit: the accounts file ──────────────────────────────────────────
accounts.json

# ── Build output and dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.gradle/
app/build/
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks

# ── Scraped data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Regenerable, and large: results/ alone runs to tens of megabytes, and one
# channel_videos CSV is over 60 MB — past what GitHub accepts without LFS.
# The scripts that produce it are what matter; the output is not source.
1_tiktok_search_scraper/results/
2_comment_automation/output/
*.csv
!sample*.csv
!*example*.csv

# The likers' ledgers: which comment each account has already liked. Per-machine
# state, and it names accounts.
done*.csv
done*.csv.bak
done*.csv.tmp

# Scratch output from the probes
inspect*.json
inspect*.png
capture.json
captcha-fail-*.png
*.log

# ── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
